{"text": "The need to sleep interferes with. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Other more biologically pressing needs. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Such as finding and gathering food. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Building shelter. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And anything else you might do. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To ensure that your genetic line lives on. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Sleep is so important. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Yet so poorly understood. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That it led one biologist to say. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If sleep does not serve an absolutely vital function. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It is the greatest mistake evolution ever made. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That function is still a mystery. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It would be nice to say. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That sleep is nothing more than the time when a body rests. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But that would not be quite right either. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> You can relax in a hammock on a beach all day long. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If you want to. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But after about twenty hours. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> You will be in pretty bad shape. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If you do not fall asleep. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And stay that way for a while. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Humans need roughly one hour of sleep. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For every two hours they are awake. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And the body innately knows. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> When this ratio becomes unbalanced. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Each hour of missed sleep one night. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Will result in deeper sleep the next. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Until the bodys sleep debt is wiped clean.", "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "e", " ", "n", "e", "e", "d", " ", "t", "o", " ", "s", "l", "e", "e", "p", " ", "i", "n", "t", "e", "r", "f", "e", "r", "e", "s", " ", "w", "i", "t", "h", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "O", "t", "h", "e", "r", " 